             "of the disease ('Die Vrsach diser khranckheit sind Vnderschidlich'), including overeating/overdrinking, "
             'anger, strong wine, sharp brain fluxes, heavy lifting, and chilling; prognosis (generally not fatal and '
             'often associated with longevity, though dangerous in weak old age, potentially leading to fever, '
             'pleurisy, stroke, or palpitations); and treatment via diet, abstention from wine and sour foods, '
             'purging/evacuation, and prescribed pills followed by mineral salt and oil.',
